#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083278 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083074 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points Where the Tangent is Horizontal or Vertical"}] :question/id #uuid "72076ddb-4a3a-530f-854c-7b1400cd9859" :question/math-academy-id "e-6240" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=t^2+3, \\quad y=-t+1, \\qquad -\\infty <     t <    \\infty.\n$$\n\nDetermine the value of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is vertical." :question/worked-solution "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm = \\dfrac{y'(t)}{x'(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is vertical if $x'(t)=0$ while $y'(t) \\neq 0 .$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\nx'(t) = 2t, \\qquad y'(t) = -1 .\n$$\n\nSolving $x'(t) = 0$ gives\n\n$$\n2t=0\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad t=0.\n$$\n\nNote that $y'(0) = -1\\neq 0.$ Therefore, we conclude that when $t = 0,$ the tangent to the curve is vertical."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186554775 :question-generator/id #uuid "3fe68cb8-7969-59bc-9787-2333e1cc8c32" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186083278.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186083613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points Where the Tangent is Horizontal or Vertical"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "511bd910-5bb8-5b0b-90bc-975fb41660b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439589} {:answer/id #uuid "8ffa6a26-0ce5-57b6-8a1c-e629b857349b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439590}] :an