wer/id #uuid "d162cfde-5987-5fd8-bdf5-7c6350a3be39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255538} {:answer/id #uuid "f6d3d2d1-db33-5eba-a8dd-406ca13f50df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255830}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6d3d2d1-db33-5eba-a8dd-406ca13f50df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255830} :answer-field/id #uuid "a3597dd1-c872-5d2d-bc36-073975f4bf30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256216}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa6201e7-5014-5e6b-8fe5-7f2f7e237473" :question/math-academy-id "q-122726" :question/problem "A curve is defined by the parametric equations \n\n$$\nx=4{t}^{5},\\,y=9t,\\,-\\infty <t<\\infty .\n$$\n\nDetermine the value of $t$ at which the tangent to the curve is vertical." :question/worked-solution "The slope $m$ of a tangent line to a curve defined parametrically is given by\n\n$$\nm=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nThe tangent line is vertical if ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ while ${y}^{′}(t)\\ne 0.$\n\nSo, we first find the derivatives of $x$ and $y:$\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=20{t}^{4},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=9.\n$$\n\nSolving ${x}^{′}(t)=0$ gives\n\n$$\n20{t}^{4}=0\\,⟹\\,t=0.\n$$\n\nNote that ${y}^{′}(0)=9\\ne 0.$ Therefore, we conclude that when $t=0,$ the tangent to the curve is vertical."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186288015 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fc81cba-b997-54bc-9e11-0a4ff130833e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Points Where the Tangent is Horizontal or Vertical"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02788049-040e-5c76-86e2-58bb6a5bbbef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "t=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284808} {:answer/id #uuid "5833d